 ## Background
-The method originates from techniques in volume rendering and computer graphics for shading discrete data. [S1, unofficial] implements it in the context of differentiable rendering (SDFDiff), where normals are needed for gradient-based optimization [S1, unofficial]. [S2] applies it to explosion field visualization to improve the Blinn-Phong lighting model's accuracy at resampling points, addressing errors from separate color/opacity interpolation [S2].
